      "created_at": "2017-02-04T09:48:06Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-02-04T09:48:06Z",
      "body": "I don't know if that is the case. For example, in my production database, right at this moment I have 1.874.532 guest customers (I haven't deleted them in a while), and only 69.957 generic attributes with EuCookieLaw.Accepted (and these are not filtered by the customer role, these are for all the customers). So not every user closes the cookie warning.\r\n\r\nBut, I agree, another possible solution would be to save a cookie just for the EUCookieLaw notification.",
